     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-10-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>1,000 Students Remove 2,000 Kg of Waste from Yamuna</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Yamuna Cleanup</span> <span>#Student Initiative</span> <span>#Delhi University</span> <span>#Environmental Protection</span></div>
       <p>On Gandhi Jayanti, 1,000 students from 15 Delhi University colleges participated in a large-scale cleanup drive, successfully removing 2,000 kg of waste from the Yamuna River. The initiative, named Gen Z Yamuna Jal Chaupal, took place at Kalindi Kunj.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/1000-students-remove-2000-kg-of-waste-from-yamuna.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The event was organized by the Green Pencil Foundation in collaboration with The Better India. Students walked barefoot to the riverbank, demonstrating their commitment, and immediately began the work of segregating wet and dry waste. Their efforts led to the removal of significant amounts of plastic, textile waste, and idols from the area.</p><p>Beyond the immediate impact of the cleanup, the drive served as a powerful reminder about the importance of civic responsibility. The organizers emphasized that civic sense is a continuous commitment, not limited to a single day. The message highlighted that the Yamuna is a shared river and Delhi a shared city, underscoring that maintaining their cleanliness is a collective responsibility, with change beginning when individuals take action rather than waiting for others.</p><p>Why it matters: Collective action can drive significant environmental change.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the source summary, covering the event, the organizers, the participants, and the core message.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/videos/1000-students-remove-2000-kg-of-waste-from-yamuna-12670763" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
