       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · ESPN Cricinfo · 2026-10-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Afghanistan holds Bangladesh to a draw following Sediqullah Atal's century</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Afghanistan secured a draw against Bangladesh after Sediqullah Atal became the first Afghan batter to record a fourth-innings century. The match concluded as Bangladesh failed to take the final two wickets, with missed chances in the final hour proving costly for the fielding side.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/afghanistan-holds-bangladesh-to-a-draw-following-sediqullah-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The result followed significant contributions throughout the test, including a century from Litton Das and a large lead established by Mushfiqur Rahim and Najmul Hossain Shanto. Despite strong performances from the Bangladesh bowlers, Afghan lower-order resistance successfully held the match to a stalemate.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief captures the essential outcome and the reasons for the draw, including the historical significance of the century.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.cricinfo.com/ci/content/story/1558264.html?ex_cid=OTC-RSS" rel="noopener">ESPN Cricinfo</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
