       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Allahabad HC Rules Misbehavior with Government Advocates is Contempt</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Allahabad High Court has directed the Uttar Pradesh Director General of Police to issue a circular warning officers that misbehaving with government advocates amounts to contempt of court. The order followed an incident where a Public Relations Officer allegedly harassed an additional government advocate, resulting in the officer being briefly held in court custody.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/allahabad-hc-rules-misbehavior-with-government-advocates-is-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Justice Arun Kumar Singh Deshwal emphasized that advocates represent the court and must be respected while ensuring compliance with judicial orders. During the same hearing, the court rejected a bail plea filed by a rape accused and addressed negligence regarding the execution of non-bailable warrants by local police officials.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise and covers the core judicial directive and the trigger incident accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
