     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-10-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Apple Music App Icon Replaced with Black-and-White Version in iOS 27.2 Beta</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Apple Music's red app icon has reportedly been replaced with a black-and-white version in the latest iOS 27.2 beta. According to 9to5Mac, the new design features a black music note on a white background in light mode, with the opposite color scheme in dark mode.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/apple-music-app-icon-replaced-with-black-and-white-version-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The eighth note on the icon also exhibits a slightly sharper angle than the original version. Additionally, Apple Music widgets now feature black backgrounds, suggesting the company is updating its visuals to match a new logo spotted last month.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate and concise summary of the provided text, capturing the core technical changes reported.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1010619/apple-music-new-icon-ios-27-beta" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
