     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>BCCI President Manhas Outlines Conditions for World Cup 2027 Selection</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#BCCI</span> <span>#World Cup 2027</span> <span>#Mithun Manhas</span></div>
       <p>BCCI President Mithun Manhas has stated that age should not be a barrier for player selection in the ICC World Cup 2027, which begins in October next year. Concerns had been raised regarding the chances of veteran players Virat Kohli and Rohit Sharma, who will be 39 and over 40 respectively during the tournament.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/bcci-president-manhas-outlines-conditions-for-world-cup-2027.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Manhas clarified that the BCCI is not in a position to comment directly on selection, as it depends on selectors and coaches. However, he emphasized that fitness and performance must be the primary criteria, not age. He further stated that if a player is fit, performing, and winning games for the country, that should be the sole focus for selection. Both Kohli and Sharma recently scored centuries in the ODI series against the West Indies, which has reportedly quieted murmurs about their futures.</p><p>Manhas believes that the presence of experienced players like Virat Kohli, Hardik Pandya, and Rohit Sharma would benefit ODI captain Shubman Gill. He also mentioned that players like Jasprit Bumrah could serve as bowling captains, highlighting the importance of workload distribution. These veterans have a proven track record of delivering in high-pressure situations, forming a strong combination.</p><p>Former India batter Mohammad Kaif also shared his perspective on the 2027 ODI World Cup, set to be played in South Africa, Zimbabwe, and Namibia. Kaif noted that playing conditions in South Africa have become more batting-friendly, suggesting that batters will likely dominate. He added that the quality of bowling attacks will ultimately determine the winner. South Africa is slated to host the two semi-finals and the final, with Cape Town, Centurion, and Johannesburg identified as the venues for these crucial matches.</p><p>What to watch: The selection policies as the 2027 World Cup approaches.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately captures all key points from the source text, including the specific quotes and context regarding World Cup 2027 selection criteria.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/bcci-chief-mithun-manhas-sets-two-conditions-for-world-cup-2027-selection-when-asked-about-virat-kohli-rohit-sharma-12177453#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
