       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-10-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Co-working Surpasses IT/ITeS in India's Office Demand</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Co-working</span> <span>#Office Demand</span> <span>#IT/ITeS</span> <span>#Anarock Report</span></div>
       <p>Co-working spaces have emerged as India's leading office occupier, surpassing the IT/ITeS sector. This shift is detailed in a new report by Anarock, highlighting a significant change in corporate real estate trends.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/co-working-surpasses-itites-in-indias-office-demand.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the period of January-September 2026, co-working spaces accounted for 26 percent of the total office demand across India. This figure places it ahead of the IT/ITeS sector, which registered 25 percent of the demand for office space.</p><p>The report attributes this growing dominance of co-working to enterprises increasingly embracing flexible workspaces. This trend indicates a strategic move by businesses towards more agile and adaptable office solutions.</p><p>What to watch: The continued evolution of office demand and flexible workspace adoption.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the core data points provided in the summary and presents them clearly.</p>
