     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-13 · editor 7/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Former Minister Dhal Singh Bisen Appointed Uttarakhand Governor</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Dhal Singh Bisen, a 74-year-old former cabinet minister and Member of Parliament, has been appointed Governor of Uttarakhand. The veteran politician, who is an Ayurvedic doctor and farmer from Madhya Pradesh, received news of his appointment while at home.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/former-minister-dhal-singh-bisen-appointed-uttarakhand-gover.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Bisen served as an MLA for multiple terms and held various portfolios in the Madhya Pradesh government, including transport and education. A member of the Pawar community, he previously served as a Lok Sabha MP from 2019 to 2024. Bisen stated he intends to serve the people of Uttarakhand with constitutional dignity and cooperate with the state government.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate but includes unnecessary biographical padding (e.g., birthdate, specific districts) not essential to the news of his appointment.</p>
