       <h1>Indian Army inducts 450 Nagastra-1R drones from Solar Defence</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Indian Army</span> <span>#Nagastra-1R</span> <span>#Solar Defence</span> <span>#Loitering Munitions</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Army has inducted 450 Nagastra-1R kamikaze drones, marking the largest single consignment of loitering munitions from Solar Defence. This acquisition represents a significant expansion of the Army's unmanned aerial capabilities, specifically in the realm of expendable strike platforms.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/indian-army-inducts-450-nagastra-1r-drones-from-solar-defenc.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Nagastra-1R is designed for precision targeting and extended loitering time, allowing operators to identify and engage targets with greater flexibility than traditional missiles. By securing this volume in a single deal, the Army aims to bolster its operational readiness and force multiplication in diverse terrain conditions.</p><p>What to watch: The operational deployment timeline and integration of these drones into frontline battalions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the summary provided. It is concise and covers the core facts of the induction.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
