     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · BS Personal Finance · 2026-10-13 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>IRCON International Shares Jump 6% on New ₹862 Crore Railway Order</h1>
       
       <p>IRCON International, a Navratna public sector undertaking (PSU), saw its shares climb over 6 per cent in Tuesday's intraday trading after securing a new ₹862.45 crore engineering, procurement, and construction (EPC) contract from the East Central Railway. The PSU rail stock reached a day's high of ₹111.45 on the BSE, up from its last closing price of ₹104.75, marking a 6.4 per cent increase in intraday deals. By 11 AM, the share price was trading at ₹105.75, up 1.15 per cent, contrasting with a 0.60 per cent rise in the BSE Sensex to 72,356.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/ircon-international-shares-jump-6-on-new-862-crore-railway-o.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The newly awarded contract, detailed in an exchange filing dated October 12, involves the supply of ballast and permanent way materials, including track laying and linking, for 32.5 T axle load sections in Gomoh-Koderma (Rly km 300.15 to 393.68, DHN Division) and Gaya-Son Nagar (Rly km 475.200 to 542.075, DDU Division) of the East Central Railway. It also includes the supply of various permanent way materials at Gaya under Dy. CE/Con/Gaya, all in connection with the construction of the 3rd and 4th lines of the Son Nagar-Andal Project. The project has a completion period of 365 days.</p><p>This order follows another recent win on September 9, when IRCON secured a ₹96.25 crore contract from Konkan Railway Corporation. That contract is for five years of comprehensive annual maintenance of the integrated tunnel communication system in the Katra-Banihal section of Northern Railway, covering IP-based video surveillance, public address, emergency communication, and networking backbone systems installed at tunnels, bridges, and stations.</p><p>For an ordinary saver or taxpayer, IRCON's new orders indicate continued government infrastructure spending, particularly in railways. This suggests ongoing economic activity in a key sector, which can support jobs and broader economic stability. While the company's stock has seen a significant decline of 40 per cent year-to-date and 39 per cent over the last year, new contracts like these contribute to its substantial order book, which stood at ₹23,366 crore at the end of the June quarter. This large order book provides revenue visibility for the company's future operations.</p><p>However, market analysts like Vipin Kumar, AVP of equity research at Globe Capital Market, suggest caution for traders. Kumar noted that the stock has been drifting lower, exhibiting a weak structure below its long-term and short-term moving averages. He identified immediate support around the ₹100-₹101 spot zone, advising traders to wait for a reversal or base formation before accumulating fresh positions, as a decisive close below ₹100 could further weaken sentiment towards ₹93-₹92 levels.</p><p>What to watch: The company's execution of new projects and its stock performance in the coming months.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft provides a thorough and accurate report on the contract win, financial performance, and analyst commentary using the provided source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
