     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Karnataka to Disburse ₹100 Crore in Pending Minority Scholarships</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Karnataka's Minister for Minorities Welfare, U.T. Khader, announced the government will clear ₹100 crore in pending minority scholarships. The department has earmarked ₹494.71 crore for scholarships this year, supporting students from class 1 through PhD levels.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/karnataka-to-disburse-100-crore-in-pending-minority-scholars.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>To improve grievance redressal, the department is launching an online helpline at 82777 99990 and a “Minority Mitra” mobile application. Additionally, the government plans to establish 100 new Shishunala Sharif schools for ₹800 crore by late November. The state has also requested the Karnataka State Open University extend fee payment deadlines for over 13,000 students awaiting financial reimbursement under departmental schemes.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the core details of the scholarship program, helpline, and school infrastructure plans.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/karnataka-to-clear-100-crore-in-pending-minority-scholarships-says-minister/article71579471.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
