     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-10-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kolte-Patil Reports 52% Q2 Sales Growth Despite Market Headwinds</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Pune-based Kolte-Patil Developers Limited reported a 52% year-on-year rise in Q2 FY27 sales, reaching Rs 1,019 crore. The growth was bolstered by the successful launch of 'Vyana at The Reserve' in Pune, which contributed Rs 616 crore in sales, alongside a 33% increase in collections to Rs 795 crore.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/kolte-patil-reports-52-q2-sales-growth-despite-market-headwi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Despite softening near-term demand in broader markets, the company expanded its Mumbai Metropolitan Region portfolio by adding six redevelopment projects with an estimated gross development value of Rs 6,000 crore. Management noted that strategic price revisions and a higher contribution from Mumbai projects improved average realization to approximately Rs 8,368 per sq. ft. during the first half of the fiscal year.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately captures the key financial data and strategic developments from the source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/kolte-patil-developers-record-sales-q2-fy27-demand-softens-126101300449_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
