       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · BBC World · 2026-10-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Missiles Intercepted Over Riyadh Following Saudi Strike on Sanaa Fuel Depot</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Missiles and drones were intercepted over Riyadh after the Saudi-led coalition struck a fuel depot near the Houthi-controlled capital of Sanaa. Maj Gen Turki al-Maliki confirmed that projectiles targeting Riyadh and other cities were intercepted following the attack on the al-Sabaha facility.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/missiles-intercepted-over-riyadh-following-saudi-strike-on-s.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The strikes followed recent deadly attacks on Saudi Arabia, prompting warnings from the Saudi cabinet that the Iran-backed Houthi group will bear the consequences. The conflict continues to escalate as both sides exchange military actions across the region.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Strong, dense summary that correctly synthesizes the complex timeline of events described in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
