       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPACE</span> · NASA · 2026-10-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>NASA Prepares SmallSats for SpaceX Falcon 9 Launch</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#space</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Three NASA-supported small spacecraft were encapsulated into a SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket for an October 1, 2026, launch. The payload includes the ASCENT Propulsion Dual Mode CubeSat, the SPRITE CubeSat, and the SSPICY mission.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/nasa-prepares-smallsats-for-spacex-falcon-9-launch.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>These satellites aim to test advanced propulsion technologies, investigate galactic dust and high-energy radiation, and improve methods for inspecting inactive satellites. The mission, part of the Transporter-18 launch, carries these research tools alongside various commercial payloads to demonstrate new capabilities in space exploration and satellite maintenance.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the mission payloads and objectives based on the provided text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.nasa.gov/image-article/transporter-18-smallsats-encapsulation/" rel="noopener">NASA</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
