     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>New Coastal Road Links Kollam to Koyilandy Harbour</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Two new bridges across the Cheriyathodu and Koothavallythodu canals have completed a coastal road linking Kollam to Koyilandy harbour. Constructed for ₹1.16 crore by the Harbour Engineering department, the concrete carriageway provides fisherfolk from Kollam, Arayankavu, and Gurukulam beach direct access to the harbour without utilizing the national highway.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/new-coastal-road-links-kollam-to-koyilandy-harbour.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This project serves as an alternative route for small vehicles during traffic disruptions. While the route connects several coastal areas, sections beyond the harbour remain incomplete or in poor condition due to sea erosion. The initiative is part of a broader state government effort to upgrade coastal infrastructure and improve connectivity for fishing communities.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the project's purpose, cost, and location details without unnecessary padding.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/two-bridges-complete-coastal-road-link-between-kollam-and-koyilandy-harbour/article71579132.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
