      <a href="/feed.xml" title="RSS">RSS</a>
      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/national">national</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Online Debate Over Durga Puja Origin Sparks Historical Scrutiny</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A viral claim attributing the origin of Durga Puja to Mithila, Bihar, rather than Bengal has ignited intense online debate. While some argue for Mithila's ancient Shakti traditions, others point to medieval Bengali records and 16th-century large-scale celebrations in Bangladesh as evidence of the festival's roots. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/online-debate-over-durga-puja-origin-sparks-historical-scrut.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Historical records confirm Bihar was part of the Bengal Presidency until its administrative separation in 1912, though this political boundary does not define the cultural origins of religious rituals. Experts emphasize that the festival's evolution from ancient worship to grand public celebration involves complex, interconnected regional histories that predate modern state identities.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief provides a balanced summary of the ongoing debate regarding the origins of Durga Puja, accurately reflecting the complexity presented in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/photogallery/cities/kolkata-news/did-durga-puja-begin-in-bihar-not-bengal-the-history-behind-the-viral-claim-ws-l-10379409.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
