       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Police seize photos of minor girls in 'Gem Granite' POCSO case</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Investigators have seized photographs of minor girls, including survivors who filed complaints, from the Chennai residence of ‘Gem Granite’ owner R. Veeramani. The discovery corroborates allegations that the octogenarian businessman exploited and sexually abused poor children. Six cases under the POCSO Act and one case of abetment to suicide have been registered against him.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/police-seize-photos-of-minor-girls-in-gem-granite-pocso-case.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Forensic experts have authenticated videos involving the victims, while investigations revealed that hidden recording cameras were purchased online by an associate. A Special Investigation Team is currently examining several police officers as part of the ongoing probe into these sensitive cases.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief provides a concise and accurate summary of the police findings and the legal status of the case.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/crucial-evidence-seized-in-pocso-act-case-against-gem-granite-veeramani/article71579932.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
