     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>'Ramayana' Unveils Jatayu Poster, Anupam Kher to Voice Legendary Bird</h1>
       
       <p>The makers of 'Ramayana' have released a new character poster featuring Jatayu, the legendary bird known for courage and sacrifice in the Indian epic. Veteran actor Anupam Kher will provide the voice for this pivotal figure, adding a familiar name to the film’s ensemble. The poster showcases Jatayu’s intense gaze and majestic form, emphasizing the character’s significance in the saga, where courage and duty are central.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/ramayana-unveils-jatayu-poster-anupam-kher-to-voice-legendar.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The newly released poster presents Jatayu in two striking visuals: one focusing on the bird’s face and sharp, determined eyes, and the other showing him with his wings spread wide. Titled “The Wings of Dharma,” the reveal reflects Jatayu’s role as a symbol of bravery and righteousness. His importance stems from his decision to confront evil, specifically Ravana during Sita's abduction, despite the known danger, rather than remaining a silent witness.</p><p>In the 'Ramayana,' Jatayu's attempt to rescue Sita ends in a tragic defeat, yet his courage makes him an important figure. His actions embody sacrifice, loyalty, and the willingness to stand up for what is right, even when success appears unlikely. The character's bravery is defined by his choice to act, irrespective of the battle's outcome, making him memorable.</p><p>Directed by Nitesh Tiwari, the adaptation of 'Ramayana' will feature Ranbir Kapoor as Lord Rama, Sai Pallavi as Sita, Yash as Ravana, Sunny Deol as Hanuman, and Ravi Dubey as Lakshman. The film is planned as a two-part series, with the first installment scheduled for a worldwide theatrical release on November 5, 2026. The second part is slated for Diwali 2027. Produced by Namit Malhotra, the project brings together performers from different film industries to retell this well-known story for a new generation.</p><p>What to watch: The first installment of 'Ramayana' in November 2026.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft comprehensively covers the character reveal, the actor involved, the plot significance, and the production details provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
