     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-13 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rohit Sharma Leads Race for Mumbai Indians Captaincy in IPL 2027</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Rohit Sharma</span> <span>#Mumbai Indians</span> <span>#IPL 2027</span> <span>#Captaincy</span></div>
       <p>Conflicting reports have surfaced regarding the leadership of Mumbai Indians (MI) for the Indian Premier League (IPL) 2027 season, with one source indicating that Rohit Sharma is a frontrunner to reclaim the captaincy. While no official confirmation has been issued by the franchise, Sports Tak suggests Sharma is at the top of the candidates being considered by the MI management as they reportedly reconsider their captaincy arrangement.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/rohit-sharma-leads-race-for-mumbai-indians-captaincy-in-ipl-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This potential development follows three seasons, from 2024 to 2026, during which Rohit Sharma served the franchise purely as a specialist batter. He had been removed from the captaincy role ahead of IPL 2024, a decision that attracted significant attention at the time due to his long association and success as MI's leader. Hardik Pandya was subsequently appointed as MI captain on December 15, 2023, replacing Sharma.</p><p>Under Hardik Pandya’s captaincy, Mumbai Indians experienced a challenging period, qualifying for the playoffs only once across three seasons. In IPL 2024, the team finished at the very bottom of the points table. This year, presumably IPL 2026, the five-time champions concluded the season at No. 9, recording just four wins and suffering 10 defeats from their 14 matches. These results appear to be a key factor in the management's reconsideration of the team's leadership.</p><p>Rohit Sharma’s captaincy record, both for MI and internationally, is notably stellar. He has led Mumbai Indians to five IPL titles, a remarkable feat he shares with MS Dhoni, achieving this landmark in fewer seasons. On the international stage, Sharma has further cemented his legacy by leading India to the T20 World Cup title in 2024 and the Champions Trophy in 2025, establishing himself as one of the most decorated captains in Indian cricket history.</p><p>As preparations for IPL 2027 progress, the situation is expected to become clearer. The franchise has yet to make any public announcement regarding the captaincy. Regardless of who is ultimately chosen to lead the Mumbai Indians next season, the overarching goal for the franchise will undoubtedly be to restore its past glory and winning ways.</p><p>What to watch: Mumbai Indians' official announcement on their IPL 2027 captain.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reports on the IPL 2027 captaincy speculation and provides the necessary context regarding MI's recent performance.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/reports-rohit-sharma-leading-the-race-for-mi-captaincy-in-ipl-2027/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mumbai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mumbai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
