       <h1>Tottenham Striker Richarlison Scores for Under-21s in EFL Trophy Match</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Out-of-favour Tottenham striker Richarlison scored an equalizing goal for the club's under-21 team during their EFL Trophy fixture at Cheltenham Town. The Brazil international has been excluded from Spurs' 25-man Premier League squad after summer moves to Everton and Vasco da Gama collapsed. Having made only one appearance this season in an August defeat at Brentford, Richarlison netted a tidy first-time finish from a right-wing cross after George Miller opened the scoring for the League Two side. Miracle Adewole subsequently put Tottenham ahead before Miller added a stoppage-time equalizer to send the match to penalties.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/tottenham-striker-richarlison-scores-for-under-21s-in-efl-tr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief provides a clear, accurate summary of the match events and the player's current status.</p>
