     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Vizianagaram Collector Orders GMR to Repair Roads Damaged by Airport Construction</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Vizianagaram Collector S. Ramsundar Reddy has directed GMR Visakhapatnam International Airport Limited to immediately repair approach roads damaged by heavy vehicles during the construction of the Alluri Sitarama Raju International Airport. The move follows reports that local villages, including Dibbalapalem and Ravada, were cut off, preventing farmers from accessing fields or transporting produce.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-13/vizianagaram-collector-orders-gmr-to-repair-roads-damaged-by.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Collector also instructed the National Highways Authority of India (NHAI) to establish connectivity between the airport and national highway service roads. NHAI officials have assured that these necessary infrastructural changes will be completed within a couple of weeks to restore access for passengers and local residents.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the Collector's directives to GMR and the NHAI regarding infrastructure and road repairs.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/after-the-hindu-report-collector-orders-gmr-to-repair-roads-damaged-in-bhogapuram-airport-construction/article71578019.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
